✅ What is Hibernate?
Hibernate is the most widely used ORM (Object Relational Mapping) framework for Java.
It is the implementation of the JPA (Java Persistence API) specification — meaning:
➡️ You write code using JPA annotations, and Hibernate handles the actual work behind the scenes.

🔍 Hibernate vs JPA
| Feature           | JPA                               | Hibernate                              |
| ----------------- | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |
| What is it?       | Specification (just an interface) | Implementation (a real framework)      |
| Who provides it?  | Jakarta EE                        | Hibernate.org                          |
| Can use alone?    | No                                | Yes (but usually with JPA annotations) |
| Used with Spring? | Yes                               | Yes, very commonly via Spring Data JPA |

🔸 JPA vs Hibernate:
| Feature  | JPA                     | Hibernate             |
| -------- | ----------------------- | --------------------- |
| Type     | Specification/API       | Implementation of JPA |
| Use      | Common interface        | Actual ORM framework  |
| Provider | Requires implementation | Is an implementation  |


✅ Hibernate Features
Maps Java objects to database tables

Automatically generates SQL queries

Manages caching

Handles transactions

Lazy/Eager loading of relationships

HQL (Hibernate Query Language)

